course: dictionary
lesson: 4997
title: Indoors and indoor
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Indoors means inside a building, not outside. It is an adverb, so it tells you where something happens: «Stay indoors during the storm.» Here the storm is outside, so you stay inside a building to be safe.
explain: Indoor is an adjective, so it describes a thing: «an indoor pool» is a pool inside a building, and indoor games are games you play when it rains.
explain: The sentences around the word give you clues. «If you hear thunder, you are close enough to be struck by lightning, so you go indoors.» Thunder warns of danger, so going indoors means going inside a building, away from the lightning.
explain: Useful phrases to remember are go indoors, stay indoors, keep indoors and indoor games.
fact: Indoors means inside a building, not outside.
fact: Indoor is the adjective, as in «an indoor pool».
fact: In a thunderstorm, go indoors, because lightning can strike a person standing outside.
fact: Keep pets indoors during fireworks, and never use a barbecue indoors because its gas can be poisonous.
fact: Children need time outdoors as well as indoors.
exercise: «If you hear thunder, you go indoors.» What does indoors mean? | Under the water | *Inside a building, not outside | Up in a tree | Far away over the hills
exercise: What kind of word is indoor in «an indoor pool»? | A noun | *An adjective | A verb
exercise: Dad says, «Never use a barbecue indoors.» Why? | *Because its gas can be poisonous | Because it is too cold to cook | Because it is too dark to see | Because the food tastes bad
test: «Winter helps the viruses because we all crowd indoors with the windows shut.» What does indoors mean here? | *Inside a building | Outside in the cold | Under the windows | Far from other people
test: Which phrase fits best? «In a storm, ___.» | Climb the tallest tree | Play outdoor sports | *Go indoors
exam: In «The indoor pool is closed today», which word is an adjective describing the pool? | today | closed | the | *indoor
